WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.780
At one time, Gwyneth Paltrow was one of Hollywood's
most famous actors.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.990
However, in recent years, she's stepped back
from the spotlight and devoted her energy

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.420
to other endeavors.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.040
Here's why you don't see Gwyneth Paltrow onscreen
much anymore.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.130
In the aftermath of Se7en and Emma, Gwyneth
Paltrow was in high demand in Hollywood, and

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:26.739
in 1998 alone, she released five movies: Great
Expectations, Sliding Doors, Hush, A Perfect

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:28.869
Murder, and Shakespeare in Love.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:33.120
Though Hush wasn't one of Paltrow's winners,
the rest became fairly big hits.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.289
Sliding Doors is still one of her most popular
and referenced performances, and of course,

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:42.969
Shakespeare in Love won Paltrow her first
Academy Award for Best Actress thanks to her

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:48.290
role as Viola, a noblewoman who carries on
a passionate affair with William Shakespeare.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.320
Paltrow suddenly became one of the industry's
biggest names, following up her Oscar win

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.109
with the crowd favorite The Talented Mr. Ripley
in 1999.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:01:00.870
However, her huge awards win might have led
to a bit of a professional downfall.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.500
After winning big for Shakespeare in Love,
Gwyneth Paltrow's career floundered, and a

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.990
string of critically panned and commercially
unsuccessful films followed her famous turn

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:11.990
as Viola.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.430
Part of that may have been backlash over the
Oscar win, and even years after the fact,

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.560
some of Paltrow's peers don't think she deserved
the trophy.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.530
In 2020, Glenn Close discussed the win, saying,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.930
"I remember the year Gwyneth Paltrow won over
that incredible actress who was in Central

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.610
Station [Fernanda Montenegro and I thought,
'What?'

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.430
It doesn't make sense."

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.950
Paltrow herself has cast doubt on the win,
saying it led to some bad choices.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.160
As reported by Reuters, Paltrow admitted,

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.180
"I think part of the downside about being
so successful and winning the Oscar at the

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.259
age of 26 is that I sort of became insouciant
about the things that I chose [...] I thought

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:52.359
'Oh, I'll just try this, it'll be fun or I'll
do that for the money'.

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:55.299
Things like that now I would absolutely never
do."

00:01:55.299 --> 00:02:00.229
Obviously, curses don't actually exist, but
it seems that the win may have gone to Paltrow's

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:02.600
head, and negatively affected her career.

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:08.610
Aside from 2001's The Royal Tenenbaums, which
is still one of Wes Anderson's most beloved

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:13.610
films, Gwyneth Paltrow's post-Oscar film choices
were definitely a bit suspect.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.590
That same year, she appeared alongside Jack
Black in Shallow Hal, a romantic comedy about

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.250
a man who starts seeing people's "inner beauty."

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.440
As such, while Paltrow's character, Rosie,
is actually overweight, Hal sees her as Hollywood

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.640
A-list thin.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.970
Though the movie performed well at the box
office, its premise was offensive even by

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:37.470
2001's standards when it comes to body-shaming
and inclusivity, and it definitely hasn't

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.940
aged well as the years have gone on.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.080
Paltrow later even called it a "disaster."

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.950
After that, Paltrow appeared in the 2003 flight
attendant romantic comedy View from the Top,

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:53.590
which Paltrow herself later called "the worst
movie ever," and followed that with 2004's

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:59.110
Sky Captain and the World of Tomorrow after
her Talented Mr. Ripley co-star Jude Law enlisted

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.290
her for a role.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.560
The film did perform well critically, but
ultimately barely earned its budget back,

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.560
adding to Paltrow's list of flops.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:13.800
Gwyneth Paltrow has taken on one hugely successful
role in recent years that spans several blockbuster

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.060
films: Pepper Potts in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.770
Introduced in the film that kicked off the
MCU, 2008's Iron Man, Pepper works as the

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:27.650
assistant and confidante for millionaire playboy
Tony Stark, played by Robert Downey Jr.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:33.700
After that, Paltrow reprised her role as Pepper
in 2010's Iron Man 2, 2012's The Avengers,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:41.500
2013's Iron Man 3, 2017's Spider-Man: Homecoming,
2018's Avengers: Infinity War, and 2019's

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.040
Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.200
Pepper may not be a main character in the
MCU, but she's vital for Tony's character

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.200
development.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.840
However, despite her long-running arc as Pepper
Potts in the MCU, Paltrow doesn't seem to

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.740
think about those films very much, to the
point where she often forgets she even appeared

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:58.740
in them.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.270
In a now-infamous moment from Jon Favreau's
cooking series The Chef Show, Favreau, who

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:09.180
appears alongside Paltrow in 2017's Spider-Man:
Homecoming, reminds her of a moment from filming

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:14.090
that movie, only for Paltrow to coolly inform
her co-star that she wasn't in the movie.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.650
"We weren't in Spider-Man."

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.409
"Yes we were."

00:04:17.409 --> 00:04:18.409
"Homecoming."

00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:20.340
"You were in Spider-Man."

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.340
"No."

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.950
Between that and the fact that, according
to Bucky Barnes actor Sebastian Stan, she

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:31.629
keeps forgetting who he is, and also doesn't
seem to know who Tom Holland, who plays Spider-Man,

00:04:31.629 --> 00:04:36.469
is either, it definitely doesn't seem like
Paltrow thinks about her Marvel projects particularly

00:04:36.469 --> 00:04:40.819
often, which indicates her acting career may
not be her priority these days.

00:04:40.819 --> 00:04:47.030
"I thought that it was an Avengers movie but
it was not."

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:51.659
Gwyneth Paltrow is passionate about clean,
healthy eating and high-quality food.

00:04:51.659 --> 00:04:57.000
In 2007, after her career had taken a bit
of a downturn, Paltrow worked with PBS for

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Spain...

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.260
On the Road Again, which sent her to Europe
to explore the country's cuisine.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.749
One year later, she released a cookbook on
Spanish food with chef Mario Batali.

00:05:05.749 --> 00:05:11.300
In 2011, she published two culinary books,
My Father's Daughter: Delicious, Easy Recipes

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:16.320
Celebrating Family and Togetherness and Notes
From My Kitchen Table, and later followed

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:21.620
those with her 2013 cookbook It's All Good:
Delicious Easy Recipes That Will Make You

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.939
Look Good and Feel Great.

00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:28.610
However, Paltrow's move into the culinary
scene was met with some controversy, especially

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:33.460
over an "elimination diet" she promoted in
her 2013 book, which didn't have a ton of

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.830
scientific evidence to back it up.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:41.419
As recently as 2020, after suffering from
COVID-19, Paltrow promoted a diet and routine

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:45.469
to supposedly help "long-haul" patients with
long term symptoms.

00:05:45.469 --> 00:05:48.580
That diet was also critiqued by medical professionals.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:54.280
Gwyneth Paltrow took a huge leap in 2008 when
she launched her newsletter, Goop.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:58.800
After the official Goop website eventually
launched, an online store was quickly born,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.979
and the critics descended upon the actress.

00:06:00.979 --> 00:06:05.360
They accused her of spreading bad scientific
information as well as seeming utterly out

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.330
of touch, as her gift guides often included
prohibitively expensive items.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:15.099
Ultimately, it seems like Goop's critics were
actually kind of vital to its success, with

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:19.080
even its most ridiculous and bizarre products
selling out regularly.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:24.180
Obviously, beyond its controversies, Goop
is a huge project, which definitely cuts into

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:29.629
Paltrow's time, and she cited it as a reason
for frequent gaps in her acting resume.

